Release	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-09-05T23:29:59.0334348Z [{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/browser-commander/pulls/84","id":4451536683,"node_id":"PR_kwDOQYTTi88AAAABCVUPKw","html_url":"https://github.com/link-foundation/browser-commander/pull/84","diff_url":"https://github.com/link-foundation/browser-commander/pull/84.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/link-foundation/browser-commander/pull/84.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/browser-commander/issues/84","number":84,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Check for all false positives, false negatives, warnings and errors in CI/CD and fix them all","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What this changes\n\nCloses #83.\n\nThe issue points at eight workflow runs on `main` at `4f7af54`: one red, seven\ngreen. The red one is real, and **two of the seven green ones were lying** —\nthe JS release crashed after bumping the version and still reported success,\nand the Rust release has published twelve versions to crates.io without ever\ncommitting the bump that produced them.\n\nThat inversion is the finding. The single defect underneath most of it is that\n`command-stream`'s `` $`…` `` **resolves** on a non-zero exit instead of\nrejecting, so every `try { await $`…` } catch { process.exit(1) }` in thirteen\nrelease scripts is unreachable code.\n\nAll evidence is committed under\n[`dev/log/issues/83/pulls/84/`](dev/log/issues/83/pulls/84/): the eight full\nrun logs, the timeline, the requirement matrix, the root causes, and the\nupstream reports.\n\n## Root causes and fixes\n\n| # | Class | Defect | Fix |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| RC-A | error | PyPI trusted publishing has no registered publisher; the Python release has never once succeeded, and the error text says only that this \"could also indicate an internal error\" | `811d1dc` — a failure explainer that names which of PyPI's two registration forms applies and what to type into it; **registering it is a maintainer action** (see below) |\n| RC-B | false negative | `command-stream`'s `$` resolves on non-zero exit, so 13 release scripts' error handling is dead code | `a2c32ba` — `shell.errexit(true)` at the shared choke point `scripts/use-module.mjs` |\n| RC-C | false negative | the Rust release publishes to crates.io without committing `Cargo.toml` or the changelog | `ec429c2` — commit gate on `git status --porcelain`; every publish step now requires `version_committed == 'true'` |\n| RC-D | error | JS and Rust both wrote `v<version>` tags and overwrote each other | `65698af` — Rust moves to a `rust-v*` namespace |\n| RC-E | false negative → false positive | the release commit is pushed with `GITHUB_TOKEN`, which by design triggers no workflow, so it is the one commit nobody tests | `44192e3` — the release job validates the commit it is about to push, in the only place that ever sees it |\n| RC-G | false negative | `changeset version` bumped, wrote the changelog, then died on `spawn deno ENOENT` before deleting the consumed changeset — and the run stayed green | `49818b9`, `43708ff` — pin `\"format\": \"prettier\"`, delete the orphaned `js/deno.json` and the double-released changeset |\n| RC-H | error | `findNextAvailableVersion` throws after 20 registry probes; the walk grew by one per release and was ~9 releases from breaking outright | fixed by construction once RC-C commits the version |\n| RC-F | — | Dependency Review reporting `skipped` on a push run | **investigated and deliberately not \"fixed\"** — `skipped` is correct there, and changing it would have added the false positive this issue exists to remove |\n\nFull write-up with quoted log evidence:\n[`analysis/root-causes.md`](dev/log/issues/83/pulls/84/analysis/root-causes.md).\n\n## Reproductions and tests\n\nEvery fix landed with a test written first. New reproductions in\n`experiments/ci-repro/` stay runnable rather than archived:\n\n| Reproduction | Shows |\n| --- | --- |\n| `repro-command-stream-exit-code.mjs` | `$` resolving on exit 1 (RC-B) |\n| `repro-changeset-deno-formatter.mjs` | `changeset version` aborting between bump and cleanup (RC-G) |\n| `repro-template-dead-catch.mjs` | the same dead `catch` in the upstream template |\n| `repro-changesets-format-detect.mjs` | `@changesets/format` picking `deno` off `PATH` |\n| `repro-actionlint-pin-drift.sh` | actionlint 1.7.7 vs 1.7.12 on the same workflow |\n\nNew unit tests (`js/tests/unit/scripts/`, run on every pull request):\n`command-stream-errexit`, `changeset-formatter`, `cargo-lock-sync`,\n`changelog-collection-order`, `check-release-format`, `ci-workflow-policy`,\n`command-error-text`, `release-tags`, `rust-changelog`, `required-docs`, plus\n`test_collect_changelog.py` and `test_explain_pypi_failure.py` on the Python\nside. `js` unit suite: **805 tests, 0 failures**.\n\n## Best practices\n\nAll fifteen principles from\n[CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/main/docs/CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md)\nare audited one by one, with the evidence for each verdict, in\n[`best-practices/audit.md`](dev/log/issues/83/pulls/84/best-practices/audit.md).\nTwo were genuinely violated:\n\n- **#5 fast-fail** — the three-OS test matrix did not wait for `lint`. Worse,\n  adding `needs: [lint]` alone would have been decorative: a status function\n  such as `!cancelled()` **overrides** GitHub's implicit \"all needs succeeded\"\n  rule, so the failure has to be restated with\n  `!contains(needs.*.result, 'failure')` (`7eea70a`, all three languages).\n- **#12 documentation validation** — half-met. `96dda92` adds\n  `scripts/check-required-docs.sh`, a `Validate Documentation` job and a\n  pre-commit hook: it checks that the required documents exist *and* that the\n  three language READMEs still carry the same six sections, which is the drift\n  `docs/feature-parity.md` exists to prevent.\n\n`e8ccea5` also moves actionlint to the `1.7.12` the document names; the older\npin reports live runner labels (`macos-15-intel`, `windows-11-arm`) as unknown\nand cannot see a `paths:` filter written `./src/**` that matches nothing.\n\n## Templates\n\nA full file-tree comparison against all three pipeline templates is in\n[`templates/file-tree-diff.md`](dev/log/issues/83/pulls/84/templates/file-tree-diff.md)\n(377 / 83 / 149 upstream paths, each CI/CD-relevant absence with a decision).\n\nTen issues were filed upstream, each with a reproduction that was executed\nbefore it was written, a workaround, and suggested code. Bodies are kept in\n[`templates/upstream-reports/`](dev/log/issues/83/pulls/84/templates/upstream-reports/):\n\n| Defect | Reported |\n| --- | --- |\n| dead `catch` around `command-stream` (RC-B) | [js#170](https://github.com/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/170) |\n| release commit never validated (RC-E) | [js#171](https://github.com/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/171), [rust#159](https://github.com/link-foundation/rust-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/159) |\n| `deno.configFiles` makes the `fmt`-key check unreachable (RC-G's true mechanism) | [changesets/format#45](https://github.com/changesets/format/issues/45) |\n| actionlint pinned five releases behind | [rust#160](https://github.com/link-foundation/rust-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/160), [js#172](https://github.com/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/172), [python#71](https://github.com/link-foundation/python-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/71) |\n| documentation validation checks existence but never content | [js#173](https://github.com/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/173), [python#72](https://github.com/link-foundation/python-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/72), [rust#161](https://github.com/link-foundation/rust-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/161) |\n\nPlus a correction on the existing\n[js#154](https://github.com/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/154#issuecomment-5555145046),\nwhich named a mechanism that is not the one that fires and a workaround that\ndoes not prevent it. The candidates that were **not** filed, and why, are\nrecorded in the same directory.\n\n## One thing code here cannot do\n\nRC-A needs a maintainer. PyPI trusted publishing has no publisher registered\nfor this repository, so the Python release fails at the upload step no matter\nwhat this branch does. The new `explain_pypi_failure.py` prints the exact\nvalues to register — owner, repository, workflow filename, environment — the\nnext time it fails.\n\n## Verification\n\n- All eight workflows are green on the head commit `31271d4`: JS, Python, Rust,\n  Repository Quality Gates, Security, Documentation, Broken Link Checker and CI\n  Workflow Policy. Every job that reports `skipped` was checked individually —\n  the release jobs (a pull request is not a release), Deploy GitHub Pages (main\n  only), and Rust's Changelog Fragment Check (`rust-code-changed` matches\n  `.rs`/`.toml` under `rust/`, and this branch changes `rust/scripts/*.mjs`).\n- `js`: `npm run lint`, `npm run format:check`, `npm run check:duplication`,\n  `npm test` (806 passing, 0 failing) — all green locally.\n- Repository gates: `scripts/check-ci-workflows.mjs`,\n  `scripts/check-file-line-limits.sh`, `scripts/check-required-docs.sh` — green.\n- The user-visible half of these fixes is written down where users read it:\n  `js/.changeset/quiet-poems-tickle.md`, `rust/changelog.d/83.fixed.md` and\n  `python/changelog.d/83.fixed.md` carry the release notes for the next release\n  of each package.\n- Every requirement from the issue is tracked, with status and evidence, in\n  [`analysis/requirements.md`](dev/log/issues/83/pulls/84/analysis/requirements.md).\n\n","created_at":"2026-09-05T15:57:20Z","updated_at":"2026-09-05T23:27:41Z","closed_at":"2026-09-05T23:27:40Z","merged_at":"2026-09-05T23:27:40Z","merge_commit_sha":"67c003cec1453f40ba0d065f0f1a6d10d24e677c","assignees":[{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos